# Verity: everything the tooling generates. A new machine runs the setup anyway,
# and committing it would pin a stale copy of a tool meant to stay current.
# VERITY.md is the exception: written by hand, and the only record of how to
# restore all of this. .verity/.snapshot/ holds byte-for-byte copies of analyzed
# files, including any secret the gate just flagged, so it must never be committed.
# Verity installs into three harnesses (Claude Code in .claude/, the AGENTS.md
# convention in .agents/, Codex in .codex/) with the same skills and hook wiring.
#
# The one exception in .verity/ is standard.yaml, the shared Standard. The
# knowledge graph under .verity/memory/ is machine-local: the service rebuilds it,
# and committing it puts generated notes in every diff and pull request.
.verity/*
!.verity/standard.yaml
.codacy/
.claude/skills/verity-*/
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.agents/skills/verity-*/
.codex/hooks.json
.codex/config.toml

.github/instructions/codacy.instructions.md
